hGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":54,"line":52,"comment_lines":["[][52]"],"review_comment":["This further tightly couples the payload of our REST API to the payload of cluster state, despite the workflow being disjoint. I think this is fine for now, but it does present some long term concern w.r.t. these objects and the tight coupling of their serialization. The mismatch between persisted state across multiple versions of ES vs. transient state in a REST API yields different expectations and want to protect against good nature changes in the REST API breaking cluster state and vice-versa. Given the impact of getting this wrong at some future point, can you follow up with something that decouples these two ? Perhaps an adaptor pattern, where today it is an identity adaption (e.g. no differences) but is explicit and tests that changes to one will not influence the other. (or just duplicate the code between them)","You\u0027re right to point out that this is an issue. I\u0027ll follow-up with an implementation of \"`ExpressionRoleMapping` in the CS\" separate from \"`ExpressionRoleMapping` in request payload\"."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/security/authz/RoleMappingMetadata.java","id":36216,"created_at":"2024-05-29T19:39:41Z","original_position":40,"side":"RIGHT","position":36,"submitted_on_commit":"776c5ba6704fb3ac688580b8ffe07fd9a5ec6483","diff_hunk":"@@ -16,22 +16,46 @@\n import org.elasticsearch.common.collect.Iterators;\n import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamInput;\n import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamOutput;\n+import org.elasticsearch.common.xcontent.ChunkedToXContent;\n import org.elasticsearch.common.xcontent.ChunkedToXContentHelper;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xcontent.ConstructingObjectParser;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xcontent.ParseField;\n import org.elasticsearch.xcontent.ToXContent;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xcontent.XContentBuilder;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xcontent.XContentParser;\n import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authc.support.mapper.ExpressionRoleMapping;\n \n import java.io.IOException;\n import java.util.EnumSet;\n import java.util.Iterator;\n+import java.util.LinkedHashSet;\n+import java.util.List;\n import java.util.Objects;\n import java.util.Set;\n \n import static org.elasticsearch.cluster.metadata.Metadata.ALL_CONTEXTS;\n+import static org.elasticsearch.xcontent.ConstructingObjectParser.constructorArg;\n \n-public final class RoleMappingMetadata extends AbstractNamedDiffable\u003cMetadata.Custom\u003e implements Metadata.Custom {\n+public final class RoleMappingMetadata extends AbstractNamedDiffable\u003cMetadata.Custom\u003e implements Metadata.Custom, ToXContent {\n \n     public static final String TYPE \u003d \"role_mappings\";\n \n+    @SuppressWarnings(\"unchecked\")\n+    private static final ConstructingObjectParser\u003cRoleMappingMetadata, Void\u003e PARSER \u003d new ConstructingObjectParser\u003c\u003e(\n+        TYPE,\n+        // serialization tests rely on the order of the ExpressionRoleMapping\n+        args -\u003e new RoleMappingMetadata(new LinkedHashSet\u003c\u003e((List\u003cExpressionRoleMapping\u003e) args[0]))\n+    );\n+\n+    static {\n+        PARSER.declareObjectArray(\n+            constructorArg(),\n+            // role mapping names are lost when the role mapping metadata is serialized\n+            (p, c) -\u003e ExpressionRoleMapping.parse(\"name_not_available_after_deserialization\", p),","submitted_line":54},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The use of `\"name_not_available_after_deserialization\"` as a placeholder for role mapping names during deserialization is correct but could lead to confusion if developers are not aware of this behavior. Consider adding a comment explaining why this name is used and what it signifies. The change in role mapping names from specific identifiers to `\"name_not_available_after_deserialization\"` should also be documented or e